  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nHigh pressure will be present over the region all this week. While a \ncoastal low will develop and lingers for multiple days, this \nhigh pressure will prevent the system from moving inland enough\nto bring precipitation to the region. In fact, the WPC Days 1-7\nQPF has no precipitation for our area and for a large chunk of \nthe eastern US. Temperatures will trend warmer starting today \nand become more seasonable. Daytime highs will be in the 50s and\n60s while lows will be in the 30s and 40s. A slight cool down \nwill be possible late in the week as a cold airmass drops in \nfrom the north, though there is uncertainty how far west that \ncolder air will extend. Skies will be clear to mostly clear \nthroughout the week. Each night, conditions may become favorable\nfor valley fog development.",
